# Cut In ({3}{R}, sorcery): "deals 4 damage to target creature. Create a Young Hero Role token attached to up to one target creature
# you control." (CR 120.3, 111.10, 303.7.) Bot2's Wall of Earth (0/6) takes exactly 4, and Bot1's Ornithopter gets the Role: Bot1's
# creature only (Bot2's Wall is refused for the second target), and the Role gives the Ornithopter (toughness 2) a counter when it
# attacks (CR 603.4). Black Lotus and a Mox Ruby pay {3}{R}. The damage's target is a creature: Bot2 is refused for it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Ornithopter
Cut In
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Wall of Earth
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Wall of Earth.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cut In.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Wall of Earth)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Wall of Earth)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Wall of Earth.Damage = 4
? Bot1.Battlefield.Young Hero.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Ornithopter; Young Hero
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Cut In; Black Lotus
